// Rare's cut multiplayer scenarios (pdz_mp_cut_scenarios, enhancement, off by
// default). tu3-base only; TU3 addresses, launch addresses in brackets. See
// docs/TU3_BASE.md ("Cut multiplayer scenarios") for the survey.
//
// Plant the Flag (Deathmatch scenario 3) is a complete sibling of Capture the
// Flag (2): its own mode class (vtable [820B8B38], 16 slots, all implemented;
// constructor sub_8244ADC0 [8243ED28], tick sub_8244AEB8 [8243EE20]) on the
// same flag-mode base (sub_8241C388 [82411280]), so it uses the same map data
// (the CTF flags and bases). TU3's match setup still builds it for scenario 3
// (sub_8233CAC8, settings +4414). A player takes their own team's flag from
// their base, carries it into an enemy base and holds A there while a meter
// fills: the base's use action calls the mode's vtable +24 (sub_8244C540
// [82440380]: participant, the base being planted on) every frame A is held;
// the tick times the hold (participant slot +1652: hold byte mode +304, start
// mode +68 slot, base mode +72 slot) and, after mode +308, the plant check
// (sub_8244C0A0 [8243FF28]) scores for the planter's team when the base is
// an enemy's, with the FLAG_PLANTED announcer cue; the flag goes home (play
// test 2026-10-20). It is hidden only by the Deathmatch scenario list
// ([0, 1, 2, 4], game data).
//
// The enable adds 3 to the Deathmatch scenario list (DARKVALUE_SCENARIO, id
// 62) wherever the list has Capture the Flag (2), right after it, through the
// four list readers (count sub_823BB748, first sub_823BB828, last
// sub_823BB8B0, value at index sub_823BBD30), and names it "PLANT THE FLAG"
// (Rare's own string in the general table). No help scene of its own. The
// setup screen shows Capture the Flag's options panel for it (ValueRead).
//
// Bots (our addition, not Rare's: Rare never finished Plant the Flag bots).
// Neither launch nor TU3 builds a team brain for scenario 3 (the per-team
// brain factory sub_82146B10 makes one only for 2 and 4) and TU3 assigns it
// no bot script (sub_82146A00), so bots just roam and fight like Deathmatch
// bots and pick a flag up only by running over it. The enable reuses the
// Capture the Flag bot code with its goals turned round:
// - both setup functions see scenario 2 while they run, so each team gets
//   the CTF bot script (32) and the CTF team brain (vtable 820901FC, tick
//   sub_8214A9F0): per team, the state of every team's flag (+16: 1 home,
//   2 held by an enemy, 3 held by us, 4 dropped), a target team (+48) and
//   three bot groups with goals set through sub_82539AA0 (3 attack the
//   carrier, 4 go to the target team's flag, 5 carry it to base, 6 return a
//   dropped flag, 7 guard the base, 8 escort our carrier, 0 roam);
// - attack: after the brain picks its target (sub_8214A5A0 / sub_8214A770)
//   the target is the team's own flag, so the first group fetches it,
//   escorts its carrier (goal 8) and the carrier gets goal 5;
// - the carrier's goal 5 asks the bot's team (sub_8251CC10, from 821C5978 /
//   821C59E4) for the base to carry the flag to: it gets an enemy team, so it
//   heads for the enemy base;
// - defence: the other two groups (sub_8214AEE0 / sub_8214B008) look at an
//   enemy team's flag instead of their own, so they guard home (goal 7) and
//   attack an enemy carrying its flag in (goal 3);
// - plant: while a bot carrying its team's flag stays in an enemy base's plant
//   zone (kPlantEnter / kPlantLeave, short exits paused, not reset) for the
//   mode's plant time (+308, 10 s), it scores through
//   the same plant check a player's plant ends in (sub_8244C0A0). The mode's
//   own hold slots are per human player (a bot's participant slot +1652 is 0,
//   the first player's), so bots are timed here.
// The groups are the CTF brain's own split.
//
// pdz_scenario_log (off by default): the mode's creation and first tick, flag
// carriers and drops, each team score the plant check writes, the
// multiplayer announcer cues, bot goal changes and bot plant attempts.
