// - property is what Sabotage itself counts (its round setup 82428D48): world
//   objects whose setup (+84) has the mode filter 19 (+49) and health above
//   0 (vtable +332); soft = 100 health or less (crates, drums);
// - each attacker bot picks the nearest live soft piece with an open pad
//   within 20 m (Rare's pad search with its "reachable" flag, which skips
//   pads whose links are all closed: the pad nearest a piece is usually
//   sealed by the property's own obstacle boxes, logs 108-109; a piece in a
//   shut base has none), spread over the
//   attackers, and goes there on Rare's goal 4 (the pad lookup above), as the
//   Protection bot hacker does; Rare's Sabotage brain resets every goal each
//   2 s (8214A2F4, there were no goals to give), skipped for these bots;
// - goal 4 with the team brain's flag (brain +257) doesn't send a bot to the
//   pad itself but to the nearest flagged pad within 70 m of it (8253A3E8,
//   pad flag bit 28: CTF approach spots; log 105: every attacker stopped
//   there, a corridor ~26 m short); skipped for these bots, so they walk to
//   the pad by the piece;
// - within 35 m, with a clear line (Rare's AI sight test 8216D3A8, the one
//   its bot perception uses for enemies: a physics ray with the
//   PDZ_HitmaskBlockAiSight mask; 821AA400, tried first, only checks for
//   characters in the way: log 105, bots shot walls) and no enemy targeted
//   (+12652), the bot aims with
//   Rare's aim point setter (8252CF58, as its teleporter hack 821C1A88 does,
//   set after the brain's update, which clears it each frame) and after
//   0.5 s presses its trigger (vtable +612, 8252E160, Rare's set trigger),
